Z||000000||Greg Piet||12-03-2000||01:44 PM||||I went over to the MR2 site as reccomended by a new member here to see how this MR-2 thing got started on Pennocks.  <P>I am ready now to spit on every MR-2 owner I see.  That got me so angry!  I could only make it to page 2 before I had to turn it off.  I remember in our MR-2 vs Fiero posts  here there were a few people who just bash the mister, but not like they bashed the Fiero.<P>I like MR-2's and I have been debating gettign one of the new ones, but if that is the general knowledge of MR-2 owners I dont think I should buy one.  <P>Since I do not want to make any mister owners  crazy on their own forum, ill put this post/comment here...<P>Just take it to track, and I'll be more than happy to show anyone that the Fiero's and MR-2's are pretty close, but more often than not the Fiero will win(STOCK AND SIMILIAR YEARS).||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||12-03-2000||02:09 PM||||I like MR2's also, but I don't fit (without the Jaws-Of-Life at least).<P>That site represents MR2 owners as a whole no more than this site represents Fiero owners. I agree that the people here are far more civil, but I would imagine the average MR2 owner isn't bashing Fieros every second(considering the MR2 was bought more by women in the beginning just like the Fiero).<P>If you like it, buy it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||12-03-2000||02:33 PM||||I know what you mean. I went to their forum and read that same post. It all started with some retarded a-hole who made a MR2 bashing site and I'm sure it pissed allot of the MR2 owners off. The guy put false data about Mr2’s and fiero’s in his web-site. This is why they are now bashing fiero's. I then read some of the other posts and it seems that there are allot of flame wars on that forum with everything, not just fiero's. I don’t see allot of that crap here! I would post some questions about MR2's over there but why bother; I'll just get flamed like every one else did so far that posted there and owns a fiero. To try and convince the Mr2 forum members that the fiero is a competitive sports car is like banging my head against the wall for three hours, It wold accomplish the same thing, nothing.  <P>What I like about this place is that most of the people here are open minded and mature about this subject, not defensive, impulsive and narrow minded. I’m not saying that all of the Mr2 forum members are like this just the one’s I encountered on the MR2 forum.  <A HREF="http://board.mr2pages.com" TARGET=_blank>http://board.mr2pages.com</A>  <BR>The guy who started this mess  <A HREF="http://www.bright.net/~debevecm/mr2/mr2.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bright.net/~debevecm/mr2/mr2.htm</A>  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||12-03-2000||03:30 PM||||Personally, I don't like MR2's (yes I have driven them) But the guy who put up that MR2 bash site was a moron. There are a few of the MR2 guys around here and they basically acted as mediator's to stop the flame wars. If you read the MR2 forum thread until the end you will notice that tempers calmed down and people started get along. Although the bashing got pretty heated I think that the relationship between the MR2 folks and us has become more of mutual respect and friendship.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||12-03-2000||03:33 PM||||  I think that you have to look at things in the proper perspective. If you were to poll the R2 owners, I bet you find that most of them are alot younger on average than the average Fiero owner. Younger people today are very unabashed and undaunted by anything that does not pertain strictly to themselves. Their visual acuity is based on the present and there is no regard given to the past or the future, they simply do not exist.Today they own an R2 and Fiero's are dirt. Tomorrow may find them owning a Fiero and the R2 will be the biggest piece of sh!t they ever owned. Just like here, the more mature tend to stay out of the wars unless directed at them. It's just the times people and there is no reason to keep getting upset about it. They will eventualy grow up and see things more realisticly. Both cars have their goods and their bads and owners are included in that. Just a shor take on the situation; OUT!<P> B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
